{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/node-logistics-s21/runs/eval-OPS-90-r1-instincts/portside-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "## ✅ OPS-90 Resolved\n\nI've successfully resolved OPS-90: \"Urgent cargo lists come out in the wrong order\"\n\n**The Problem:**\nThe `urgentFirst()` function in `src/schedule.mjs` was sorting cargo entries by ascending priority (smallest first), when it should return them sorted by descending priority (largest/most urgent first).\n\n**The Fix:**\nChanged the sort comparator on line 8 from `a.priority - b.priority` to `b.priority - a.priority`, reversing the sort order.\n\n**Verification:**\n- ✓ Fix matches acceptance criteria: entries with priority [1, 3, 2] now return as [3, 2, 1]\n- ✓ All 12 tests pass\n- ✓ Commit created: `a67840f`", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9TKz99D5R1hHvGDk6B", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "ba2fd9ae-9181-44e6-b218-78049d8df1d8", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:42:59.011Z", "type": "assistant"}
